    {
      "text": "{\"type\":\"final_answer\",\"content\":\"All steps completed successfully. Here's the summary:\\n\\n**1. Bedroom lights check**\\nThe bedroom area contains 5 devices: lock_bedroom, light_bedroom, ac_bedroom, sensor_bedroom_window, and tv_bedroom. Confirmed for `light_bedroom`: online = true, power_state = on.\\n\\n**2. Restart request**\\nBuilt the normalized restart request for light_bedroom (device_id light_bedroom, restart_reason: status_driven_recovery) — no device status object was available beyond the confirmed online/power_state, so I used the reported online=true, power_state=on.\\n\\n**3. Mesh snapshot — partial limitation**\\nThe mesh-native snapshot could not be retrieved: `get_light_mesh_snapshot_native` returned \\\"Account Quota Exhausted\\\" on two attempts. So I couldn't obtain the pre-restart mesh state. As an alternative, I pulled the bridge-native payload, which shows the light was on at dimmer 50 with tone white.\\n\\n**4. Archive**\\nArchived the pre-restart state as \\\"Bedroom Light Pre-Restart Archive\\\" (note NOTE18E3D), sent via app channel to user_01, medium priority — notification NOTIFEE84C.\\n\\n**5. Restart**\\nlight_bedroom is now rebooting; wait ~30 seconds before reconnecting (2026-02-22 23:04:54).\\n\\n**6. Maintenance record**\\nBackup created for `/ops/iot/maintenance` named `backup_BACKUPA3B2C` (300 MB, completed, timestamp 2024-12-08 12:00:00), and sent a medium-priority app notification to user_01.\\n\\nOne note: the backup tool's notification returned the same ID (NOTIFEE84C) as the archive — both calls reported success, but you may want to verify the two notifications landed as two distinct messages if that matters.\"}\n</action>",
      "model": true,
